<title>PERU: Peru net int'l reserves rise to $8.413 bln Oct 23.</title>
<headline>Peru net int'l reserves rise to $8.413 bln Oct 23.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Central Reserve Bank said Friday its net international reserves rose to $8.413 billion in the week ended October 23 from $8.354 billion a week earlier.</p>
<p>The bank's foreign exchange position, or total liquidity minus short-term and long-term debt obligations, stood at $1.649 billion.</p>
<p>International reserves were $6.641 billion at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>-- Eduardo Orozco, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
